<table class="gallery-text" style="width: 100%;">
<thead>
<tr>
<th class="ou-help mceNonEditable">Gallery Item - Text</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>

<h3>How Success Is Measured&nbsp;</h3>
<ul>
<li>Student retention and graduation rates&nbsp;</li>
<li>Career placement&nbsp;</li>
<li>Interdisciplinary enrollment&nbsp;</li>
<li>Research expenditures&nbsp;</li>
<li>Faculty awards&nbsp;</li>
<li>Industry partnerships&nbsp;</li>
<li>Startup activity&nbsp;</li>
<li>Philanthropy&nbsp;</li>
<li>Rankings&nbsp;</li>
<li>Economic impact&nbsp;</li>
</ul>
<h3>STRATEGIC PRIORITY: LEAD IN STUDENT SUCCESS, ACCESS AND CAREER READINESS&nbsp;</h3>
<p>Establish the college as a national model for AI, cybersecurity and computing education through future-ready curricula that adapt quickly to technological change and ensure every graduate is career-ready.&nbsp;</p>
<h4>Strategies&nbsp;</h4>
<ul>
<li>Academic programs and upskilling &ndash; Grow and ensure AI-integration in core majors (cyberecurity, AI, computer science, information technology, computer science and engineering); curricula grounded in computer science and cybersecurity engineering fundamentals as AI is built upon the enduring discipline of computer science; integrate ethics-by-design; launch computer science and engineering major, and interdisciplinary computing degrees; seek accreditation, expand concentrations, minors and stackable certificates; offer no‑code/low‑code/high‑code upskilling for non-computer science learners.&nbsp;</li>
<li>Enable student progression &ndash; Build semester schedules that are tied to student graduation plans, reduce class section sizes, provide targeted success coaching for retention, expand AI-based learning opportunities, and efficiently use TA support.&nbsp;</li>
<li>Tech Career Advancement Program (tCAP): Implement and operationalize the career advancement program. tCAP will integrate advising, experiential learning and employer partnerships into every stage of a student&rsquo;s academic journey, ensuring students graduate with strong technical foundations and applied skills, professional networks and the confidence to succeed in a rapidly evolving tech landscape.&nbsp;</li>
<li>Faculty development: Support faculty with training in emerging technologies and teaching innovation to ensure instructional excellence.&nbsp;</li>
<li>Predictive advising: Move from &ldquo;clinic&rdquo; based advising to a more proactive/predictive advising model; each student has a designated primary advisor; graduation plans for all at all time; monitor mid-term grades in all undergraduate courses, identify at-risk students, provide outreach to them, and refer them to tutoring support; identify, reach out to, support, and monitor graduates for the following two semesters; implement rule where student non-response or inaction results in a registration hold, starting as early as at the end of the first year.&nbsp;</li>
</ul>
<h4>Success Indicators:&nbsp;</h4>
<ul>
<li>Retention: Maintain first-year retention rate of &gt; 94% and academic progress rate (2nd-year retention with GPA &ge; 2.0) of at least 92%.&nbsp;</li>
<li>Four-year graduation rate (FTIC): Maintain or exceed the USF institutional goal of 70%, ensuring the college contributes to the system-wide goal of 70%&nbsp;</li>
<li>Experiential learning: Achieve 100% undergraduate participation in experiential learning.&nbsp;</li>
<li>Degrees awarded in strategic emphasis: Track the number of degrees awarded in STEM fields (CIP 11), ensuring 100% alignment with the Board of Governors' Programs of Strategic Emphasis.</li>
</ul>
<h3>STRATEGIC PRIORITY: STRENGTHEN FACULTY CAPACITY AND RESEARCH IN AI AND CYBERSECURITY&nbsp;</h3>
<p>Elevate USF&rsquo;s status as a top-tier institution in AI and Cybersecurity research by recruiting world-class faculty and building an agile, resilient, and ambitious collaborative research culture.&nbsp;</p>
<h4>Strategies&nbsp;</h4>
<ul>
<li>Recruit world-class faculty: Execute strategic high-quality faculty recruitments in AI, cybersecurity and computing to build critical mass for large-scale grants via cluster hires, targeted hiring and regular hiring.&nbsp;</li>
<li>Center-level grants: Pursue large-scale (&gt; $5 million) funding with Bellini College faculty as principal investigators by leveraging the new college structure to unify dispersed research efforts and address convergent problems responsibly and ethically; provide college-level travel funds for envisioning workshops for these grants.&nbsp;</li>
<li>REU sites: Increase the number of National Science Foundation REU Site grants; leverage resources at CRA to structure undergraduate research programming; leverage external funds, such as from CRA, FHTC.&nbsp;<br />Network building: Build partnerships with funded AI/cybersecurity institutes across the nation; engage top faculty members from other universities in proposal studios and external red‑team reviews.&nbsp;</li>
<li>Ph.D. recruitment: Build recruitment strategies for domestic students; offer multiple-year offers for high-quality students; leverage university-level scholarships.&nbsp;</li>
<li>Centers and institutes: Formulate governance and faculty-hiring policies for centers and institutes in the college; nurture the AI+X Institute and CITA; establish a center/institute for cybersecurity research and education; launch a fourth center or institute on an appropriate topic; encourage annual symposia.&nbsp;</li>
<li>Nominate faculty for external awards: Utilize USF Awards and Honors resources to nominate faculty for external awards and honors; invite speakers who are National Academy members for campus visits.&nbsp;</li>
</ul>
<h4>Success Indicators&nbsp;</h4>
<ul>
<li>Total annual research expenditures: Track growth from the current $4 million baseline to $10 million, comparable to the top 25 public computing units.&nbsp;</li>
<li>Faculty awards: Number of faculty members inducted into National Academies (preeminence metric) or receiving highly prestigious awards (e.g., NSF CAREER, Fellows of ACM, AAAS, or IEEE).&nbsp;</li>
<li>Undergraduate research: Secure faculty commitment for 100 Research Experiences for Undergraduates (REU) per year.&nbsp;</li>
<li>Ph.D. students: Build a resilient and sustainable doctoral program by achieving a target enrollment of five Ph.D. students per tenure-track faculty member.&nbsp;</li>
<li>Faculty headcount growth: Track recruitment toward the target of 100 total faculty (75 tenure-track and 25 instructional) within five years to stabilize student-to-faculty ratios.&nbsp;</li>
<li>National ranking: Achieve and maintain a Faculty Scholarly Productivity Index that places the Bellini College within the top 25 of U.S. public computing units as benchmarked by Academic Analytics.&nbsp;</li>
</ul>
<h3>STRATEGIC PRIORITY: EXPAND THE "HUB AND SPOKE" ACADEMIC ECOSYSTEM&nbsp;</h3>
<p>Democratize computing education across the university, connecting the technical "Hub" with multidisciplinary "Spokes" to increase enrollment and interdisciplinary competence.&nbsp;</p>
<h4>Strategies</h4>
<ul>
<li>Interdisciplinary majors: Launch new "+ X" joint majors to attract students from outside traditional engineering fields.&nbsp;</li>
<li>Enable joint appointments: Create "MOU templates for joint hires" with cross-college grant credit at 25%, 49%, 51%, and 75% appointment in Bellini College. &nbsp;<br />Recruitment outreach: Improve visibility by engaging high schools, community colleges, four-year colleges and industry partners.&nbsp;</li>
<li>Flat governance: Maintain a flat administrative structure to minimize bureaucracy and facilitate faster curriculum approval and affiliate faculty appointments.&nbsp;</li>
<li>Instructional capacity: Hire additional instructional faculty to support the expansion of certificates and badges.&nbsp;</li>
</ul>
<h4>Success Indicators&nbsp;</h4>
<ul>
<li>Interdisciplinary degrees awarded: Number of degrees awarded in "+ X" joint majors to measure the effectiveness of the "Spoke" integration.&nbsp;</li>
<li>Cross-college research awards: Dollar value of research grants and contracts involving faculty from Bellini College co-investigating with faculty from other USF colleges and units.&nbsp;</li>
<li>Affiliate faculty engagement: Number of non-Bellini faculty holding affiliate or joint appointments with the college to measure the effectiveness of true collaboration.&nbsp;</li>
<li>Non-computing student upskilling: Number of non-computer science majors completing courses, minors, certificates, or "boot camps.&rdquo;&nbsp;<br /><br /></li>
</ul>
<h3>Strategic Priority: Industry and Operational Excellence&nbsp;</h3>
<p>Establish Bellini College as a financially robust, operationally elite, and industry-integrated engine. This goal ensures long-term viability through optimized infrastructure, including computing and efficient operations, while serving as the primary talent pipeline for Florida&rsquo;s tech economy, targeting the "Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services" and "Manufacturing" sectors from the BOG&rsquo;s Iconic Companies list.&nbsp;</p>
<h4>Strategies&nbsp;</h4>
<ul>
<li>AI governance, policy and compliance readiness: Establish a college-led capability to operationalize emerging state and federal requirements and expectations for AI systems used in education, research and administration, including
<ol style="list-style-type: lower-roman;">
<li>transparency/&ldquo;AI interaction&rdquo; notice</li>
<li>privacy controls and deidentification standards</li>
<li>youth/parental protections where applicable</li>
<li>secure procurement and access restrictions related to foreign entities and foreign AI products or services</li>
</ol>
</li>
<li>Set execution cadence: Define an annual review cadence and a public dashboard (owners + KPI definitions) to align with the plan&rsquo;s metric ambition.&nbsp;</li>
<li>Strategic philanthropy and partnerships: Fundraise for the new building construction, specific laboratory spaces, and endowed faculty chairs to ensure long-term revenue streams. Appoint dedicated faculty or staff to serve as bridges for the Strategic Alliance, connecting corporate partners directly with student talent and research capabilities.&nbsp;</li>
<li>Infrastructure and operational excellence: Formalize the College Operations &amp; Resource Efficiency with AI group to increase operational efficiency through robotic process automation and AI-agent technology. With industry input, construct a purpose-built AI/Cyber facility and a Teaching Security Operations Center to centralize operations and attract industry funding; Build scalable compute, secure data environments, and modern collaborative spaces for shared services.&nbsp;</li>
<li>Career and innovation ecosystem: Use the Tech Career Advancement (tCAP) to connect student organizations with industry leaders. Expand mentorship, internship and co-op opportunities with industry partners. Provide direct support for student product development and faculty tech transfer through the Student Innovation Incubator at the USF Research Park.&nbsp;</li>
<li>Communication and marketing: Establish a unified brand strategy to market the new college nationally and internationally; showcase faculty expertise and research impact through targeted campaigns; improve visibility with outreach to high schools, community colleges and industry partners.&nbsp;</li>
<li>Student recruitment: Signature competitions (AI/cyber); high school recruitment; Admitted Student Day; graduate student recruitment from four-year colleges in the U.S.&nbsp;</li>
</ul>
<h4>Success Indicators&nbsp;</h4>
<ul>
<li>Financial sustainability: Surpass the college's operational costs through increased net tuition, external research grants and contracts, targeted fundraising, and naming campaigns.&nbsp;</li>
<li>Asset optimization: Achieve high utilization of the new building with a minimum of 40 hours/week and 60% occupancy.&nbsp;</li>
<li>Talent and innovation pipeline: Ensure 100% participation in internships, capstones or clinical research cases for graduating students; scale the number of active partners in tCAP; contribute to the university&rsquo;s annual goal for start-up creation through faculty and student innovation.&nbsp;</li>
</ul>
<h3>Turning Strategy Into Action&nbsp;</h3>
<p>The Bellini College strategic plan is a living framework supported by annual reviews, KPI dashboards, accountable ownership and continuous engagement with stakeholders. Progress will be measured through academic, research, operational and economic impact outcomes.&nbsp;</p>
<table class="two-column-text">
<thead>
<tr>
<th class="ou-help mceNonEditable" width="50%">Column 1</th>
<th class="ou-help mceNonEditable" width="50%">Column 2</th>
